## TokenLighten MCP (compact)

`AGENTS.md`: designs/plan. Generate AI rules from templates; never edit generated blocks.

Three tools: `tl_read_file`, `tl_edit_file`, `tl_search_files`. FIRST file lookup/read: `tl_read_file {query:"<entire user request, verbatim>",task:{epoch:"new"}}` before native/Explore subagents. Unknown paths: omit `targets`. Never shorten query to keywords or drop citation/constraint sentences. Native if the user requests native, TL is unavailable/host reports native-bypass, or incomplete scope/verified absence; never activate TL mid-task. Same-task narrow re-packs may be incomplete. Search: `action:"find",queries:["<one identifier>"]`; batch `queries=[…]`; `scope.path`=known subtree, else repo-wide.
<!-- tl-legacy-compat:start -->
Legacy only: `mode`/`paths`/`handles`/`maxBytes`/`maxTokens`/`taskProfile`/`taskEpoch` require TL_LEGACY_INPUT=accept; RC uses refuse. Never emit them; returned `next` is canonical.
<!-- tl-legacy-compat:end -->
Every call: own `cwd` (else `cwd-required-for-edit`); shared workspace: fixed `lane`. New task: `task.epoch:"new"`; continue via returned `task.id` as `task.handle`; `expected_state_version` only with that handle. User-declared read-only=`task.profile:"answer"`, change=`"generic"`; otherwise omit, never infer hints. Known single edit: use prepared `handle/search/replace`, `precondition:"unique-match"`, `allowPathFallback:false`; else ONE `tl_edit_file` `edits[]` batch, own target/item.
An unrecognized `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report it, issue no edit, never infer from its fields.
Act on `read.task_pack`'s `decision.kind`: `act.answer`/`act.edit` closes discovery; `evidence[].body` is exact source already read: use its paths/line ranges, no re-read; batch ready independent reads in ONE `targets:[...]` call and edits once. A `refusal`'s `retry` is the only transition. Every `next` is a whole executable call — run verbatim; hints are advisory, not calls. Lost context => same call with `task.force_serve:true`. A `read.receipt` is never a re-pack cue: follow `next` when present, otherwise act or stop on restated evidence/certificate. Stop after a passing relevant check. Reads accept `budget.bytes`/`budget.tokens`.
New files/tests: `edits:[{path,create:true,content}]` with explicit `cwd`; empty frontier+`create_target` means create now. Edit only served bytes this epoch. `edit.applied`=landed; `edit.rolled_back`=nothing landed; `edit.state_unknown`=>run `recovery` first. Never retry a failed edit verbatim (recorded `operation_id` replay is safe). Verification kit `omitted`=>run its batched `next` before compile/tests; discharge `recipe.gaps`. Shell: build/tests/git only; never replace TL-readable reads/searches with shell/native tools. Deep rules arrive on-demand.
<!-- tokenlighten:mcp-instructions:end -->
